From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app: the frame limit of the game's options

bare_app can hold a game to at most so many frames a second (the Options
tab of its controls screen, game_ipc.h frame_us). The link waits for it
before each frame it publishes or reports as unchanged: game_shm_pace()
of bare_app's game_ipc.h.

--- a/client/renderSDL/BareAppLink.cpp
+++ b/client/renderSDL/BareAppLink.cpp
@@ -684,6 +684,10 @@
 	const Point screenSize = std::exchange(captured, Point(0, 0));
 	if(screenSize == Point(0, 0))
 		return;
+	// bare_app's frame limit (the game's options): no sooner than that
+	// after the frame before, changed or not
+	static game_pace pace;
+	game_shm_pace(shm, &pace);
 	auto * frame = static_cast<uint32_t *>(game_shm_frame(shm, back));
 	drawCursor(frame, screenSize);
 
